# Minimal, Focused Changes

- Prefer minimal, focused changes.
- Avoid unnecessary refactoring.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Preserve existing functionality and established patterns.
- Avoid introducing new dependencies unless genuinely necessary.
- Do not make architectural changes without first discussing them.
- Preserve existing formatting conventions.

When fixing a bug or adding a feature, match the surrounding code’s naming, structure, and abstractions. Reuse existing helpers rather than reimplementing similar logic.
